It is a legendary champion, and it has added so much to these teams in the past, just like this week.
I probably didnn't see him playing two games.
I was planning more, but that's how it happened, and that's how we thought we had to proceed.
He wants to be out there, like everyone else."
On Sunday, Mickelson broke Nick Faldo's record for as many Ryder Cup gamblers.
