Red tidal tamp: Decreased concentrations at Pinellas, Manatee and Sarasota
The most recent report of the Florida Fisheries and Fauna Commission indicates a general decrease in red tide concentrations in some areas of the Tampa Bay area.
According to the CPF, more erratic blooming conditions are reported in Pinella, Manatee, Sarasota, Charlotte and Collier counties, raising fears of decreasing concentrations.
The red tide covers about 209 km (130 miles) of coast, from the north of Pinellas to the south of the counties of Lee.
Islets are found about 16 km (10 miles) off Hillsborough County, but in fewer sites than last week.
The red tide has also been observed in Pasco County.
Moderate concentrations were reported in or off Pinellas County were reported last week, low-to-high concentrations off Hillsborough County, higher concentrations in Manatee County, higher concentrations in Sarasota or offshore county, average concentrations in Charlotte County and low concentrations in and off Lee Count County, high concentrations at the bottom or offshore.
Respiratory irritation persists in Pinella, Manatee, Sarasota, Lee and Collier counties.
Respiratory Irritated in Northwestern Florida during the past week.
